    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "813cd714_33d5f825",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T06:11:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t it be better to do the detection and the setting lazily when `get_hypervisor()` is called the first time?\n\nThat way, we can ensure that clients never get an invalid hypervisor.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3f8299782b52da68727d0cb006ec65dbbb832fb0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1af053a_a9f693a2",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1984376
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T06:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That may need slowdown get_hypervisor() a bit? Everytime we need to check if this is the first time get_hypervisor() is called - and then initialize it. \n\nPerhaps make HYPERVISOR to be an option type which is initialized to None and unwrap in get_hypervisor should panic if get_hypervisor() is called before detect_hypervisor() initializes it?",
      "parentUuid": "813cd714_33d5f825",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3f8299782b52da68727d0cb006ec65dbbb832fb0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d642c881_a7284fbc",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T07:14:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s an option type, we could do something like this:\n\n```\nstatic mut HYPERVISOR: Option\u003cHypervisorBackend\u003e \u003d None;\n\nfn detect_hypervisor() -\u003e Result\u003cHypervisorBackend\u003e {\n    match query_vendor_hyp_call_uid() {\n       KvmHypervisor::UUID \u003d\u003e Ok(HypervisorBackend::Kvm(KvmHypervisor)),\n       OtherHypervisor::UUID \u003d\u003e Ok(HypervisorBackend::Other(OtherHypervisor)),\n       uuid \u003d\u003e Err(...),\n    }\n}\n\nfn get_hypervisor() -\u003e Result\u003c\u0026\u0027static dyn Hyp\u003e {\n    // SAFETY - blah\n    unsafe {\n        match \u0026HYPERVISOR {\n            None \u003d\u003e {\n                HYPERVISOR \u003d Some(detect_hypervisor()?);\n                get_hypervisor() // try again\n            },\n            Some(HypervisorBackend::Kvm(h)) \u003d\u003e Ok(h),\n            Some(HypervisorBackend::Other(h)) \u003d\u003e Ok(h),\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThere will be no performance penalty because there will be only one match for the happy case.",
      "parentUuid": "f1af053a_a9f693a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3f8299782b52da68727d0cb006ec65dbbb832fb0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
